Z||000000||NextGen||01-07-2001||03:27 AM||||Happy Newyear everybody !!!<P>I like the Fiero, but the Ferrari 348 Spider even more, but this last one is way out of my league ($$$$$$). <P>So the next best thing for me is to build a Ferrari kitcar out of a dented Fiero, but I don't have any exp. with this. <BR> So I would like to know if anyone can help me out and give me some pointers on the subject (Preferably someone from Europe), as that is where I plan to build the car and mayby buy the parts for the 348 Spider (from FieroFactory - UK) or Finale/Fino (from V8Archie - USA). <P>Thx a mill,<P>NextGen||||reg||5
Z||000001||rogergarrison||01-07-2001||09:09 AM||||ive got a 308 rebody on my Fiero. If you dont have to stretch frame its really pretty ez, just a matter of unbolting and bolting. I had my body "on" in just a couple weekends. Id def suggest you buy your kit in europe since thats where you are. Ive heard stories of stuff tied up in customs for months between usa and europe. Shipping would prob be almost as much as kit and theres the registration prob. with a kit is your car a kit or is it now an import.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||1
